  KNN Classifier - model seemed to be utilized properly by idetifying the countries with the highest ranks and grouping them together in order to properly identify the continent with the highest count.
  
  Random Forest  - we utized this method with classifying in order to aggregate the countries with highest overall life ranks, incoporate the proper questions and grab the continent associated with target and support the accuracy. Even though the model stated "Africa" and came out with an accuracy of 1, why does Africa have the lowest overall life expectancies ages? From looking at the question again, this model returned the information that it was programmed to BUT not what the target variable needs to accomplish. Techincally Africa does have the most countries with the "highest ranks" of overall life BUT the "ranks" are misconstrued and the lower the rank the better.

